# tanban-cursor project conventions

## Documentation

Normative behavior lives in `tanban-cursor-spec.md`. When behavior changes
(webhooks, label dispatch, Cursor/TanBan integration, config, persistence,
CLI, security), update in the **same change set**:

- `tanban-cursor-spec.md` — normative product/API behavior (MUSS/SOLL/KANN)
- `README.md` — if operators need different setup or run instructions

Do not leave Spec/README stale relative to the implementation. If a change
is intentionally out of scope for the current Soll, document it under
„Bekannte Lücken“ in the Spec instead of silently drifting.

## Language

- **English:** code, log messages, CLI output, commit messages
- **German:** chat with the user (proposals, questions, summaries)
- Spec and README may stay German to match TanBan sibling docs

## Architecture

- Domain logic in `app/tanban-cursor/services/`
- `routers/` and `manage.py` call services; do not duplicate dispatch/label rules there
